# Source: https://github.com/igvteam/igv/issues/890
# Symptom: name field (col 4) contains literal space characters. The validator's
# name check (length 1-255) passes since space is a valid name character per spec
# in a tab-separated file. Rejection under --spec hts is on the float score, not
# on the name; downstream tools that re-split on whitespace will misparse it. (old: "strong
#   GGGCGGGTGGGGCGGG"); parsers that tokenise on any whitespace instead of
#   strictly on tabs split the name at the space, causing col 5 to receive
#   the second word and col 6 (strand) to receive what was col 5.  The feature
#   appears with no direction arrows in IGV; bedtools may shift downstream
#   fields producing a strand field of "0.81" (a score, not a strand symbol).
chr1	1051161	1051177	strong GGGCGGGTGGGGCGGG	0.81	+
chr1	2100000	2100032	motif CCGCCCACCCCCGCCC	0.75	-
chr2	500000	500020	site with spaces here	1000	+
